=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play backup-restore ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, a mock: the restore of a backup run (P-19), a later$
# unit's, on the real plan/apply engine against a simulated$
# host; its control is the gallery's. hardn's Backup Runs is$
# read only. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: backup-restore$
# web-01.example.net is the runs host: three earlier changes$
# backed up to /var/backups/hardn. Each run leads to its files$
# and a Restore, which this mock adds to hardn's run screen.$
$
# Backup Runs ##################################################$
$
  Select a run$
$
   1) 2026-10-19 14:30     1 file, taken anyway$
   2) 2026-10-18 09:15     2 files$
   3) 2026-10-17 08:30     1 file$
$
